# WS1-07/WS1-09. Source: as 050; the hosted-amiga-13 profile provides the 20
# modules of spec/appendix-amiga.md §1 (core plus the Kickstart 1.3 surface). All
# must build and run on that profile with the debug and release lines.
profiles: hosted-amiga-13
# Seeded defect (contrast): a user ffi block redeclares a shim function with a
# different return type; the C build must then fail.
expect: output
# Amended contrast (2026-11-25, red check): the original seed was
#   contrast: func main(): i32 { ==> ffi probe {\n    func cl_dos_ticks(): u16;\n}\n\nfunc main(): i32 {
# clc rejects it with E11101 before any C is emitted (an ffi name may be declared
# once across the program), so it never reaches the C compiler. The new seed
# declares libc strlen (declared by the shim's <string.h>) with a different
# return type; the C build must fail with conflicting types.
contrast: func main(): i32 { ==> ffi probe {\n    func strlen(s: cstring): u16;\n}\n\nfunc main(): i32 {
contrast-expect: build-fails
--- output
all modules
